                            cofactor comes free. 14 is struck at 2.
    FALL        at gpf(N)   the sieve is FINISHED with N. 14 drops at 7.
  The leaf hangs while any factor is unresolved ⟹ THE FALL IS AT gpf.
  Not a stylistic choice: SMOOTHNESS IS DEFINED BY THE GREATEST PRIME
  FACTOR (N is y-smooth ⟺ gpf(N) ≤ y), and smooth relations are the engine
  of GNFS, the quadratic sieve, CFRAC and index calculus. The tree's own
  criterion is the one the field already runs on.

THE FALL-TIME DISTRIBUTION (Dickman 1930), native to the screw axis
because u is a RATIO OF LIFTS:
