THE FAMILY IDENTITY IS EXACT ON THE SCREW (not gematria's coincidence):
    ln p₁ + ln p₂ = ln N
    ln p₁ = ½ln N − δ,  ln p₂ = ½ln N + δ,  δ = ½ln(p₂/p₁)
  δ IS THE ENTIRE HIDDEN CONTENT OF A SEMIPRIME. Same object as the BKT
  unbinding threshold and the B₂≅ℤ winding, reached a third way.

WHY BALANCED RSA IS HARD: the two falls are separated by exactly 2δ.
  Unbalanced ⟹ far apart, the early event hands you everything.
  Balanced ⟹ δ→0 and BOTH FALLS COLLAPSE ONTO ½ln N. No early event to
  catch. Not "the search space is large" — THE TWO OBSERVABLES COINCIDE.

COST, kept in the record: lpf/gpf are trial division O(√n); harvest_curve
and psi_smooth are O(X log log X) time, O(X) memory. TRACKING THE FALL IS
CHEAP; REACHING IT IS NOT — for a 2048-bit modulus, observing the event
still means sieving to 2¹⁰²⁴. Naming the event correctly does not move the
wall. It puts the target on the function the field already uses, in the
coordinate the screw already speaks, with a known distribution attached.

