# THE NEGATIVE SPACE — μ, Mertens, and the three motions
# archimedes_screw v0.3, 2026-08-05
# ------------------------------------------------------------
ψ counts what ACCUMULATES; it had no counterpart for what is EXCLUDED.
The sieve is exclusion: you never test primality positively.

    GROWTH      ζ(s)   = Σ n⁻ˢ     = ∏(1 − p⁻ˢ)⁻¹
    EXTINCTION  1/ζ(s) = Σ μ(n)n⁻ˢ = ∏(1 − p⁻ˢ)

  Same product, inverted exponent. μ = the Dirichlet inverse of 1,
  Σ_{d|n} μ(d) = [n=1]. Legendre's sieve IS μ.

    ψ(x) = Σ_{pᵐ≤x} ln p   the BULK      ψ(x) ~ x
    M(x) = Σ_{n≤x} μ(n)    the MERTENS   RH ⟺ M(x) = O(x^{½+ε})

  THE SAME ½, on the exclusion side. Verified: M(10)=−1, M(100)=1,
  M(1000)=2, M(10000)=−23.

THREE MOTIONS, NOT TWO (resolves the lpf/gpf tangle — opposite polarity):
    GROWN       ζ orders; the leaf is placed at ln N
    EXTINCT     μ excludes; struck WITHOUT NAMING      at lpf  (negative)
    IDENTIFIED  the N-shape NAMES the factors          at gpf  (bulk)
  Between them the leaf is DEAD BUT UNNAMED, interval ln(gpf/lpf) = 2δ.
  Balanced RSA: δ→0, ALL THREE coincide at ½ln N.
  A prime is the degenerate case — grown, extinct and identified at once.
